Generate exactly 7 FRESH replacement VILLAGE-001B examples for member V-G10-B.

Ancestral lineage: G10
Sibling specialization: local_tinkerer
Specialization pressure:
Local tinkerer sibling: overweight bounded local memory, mundane low-stakes habits, maintenance choices and physical interaction. Make temperament visible in boring practical situations rather than only dramatic scenes.

These rows fill only missing slots from a partially salvaged chunk.
Required surface counts:
{"local_memory": 3, "mundane_low_stakes": 3, "physical_reaction": 1}

Return JSON only as {"examples":[...]}.
Every row requires: surface, input, target, generic_bad_target, why_bad, trait_refs, seed_refs.
- trait_refs: 1-5 IDs from SOURCE.trait_catalog;
- seed_refs: 0-3 valid S* IDs only;
- every input must be fresh and distinct from all forbidden inputs below;
- targets should usually be 1-5 sentences and under about 120 words;
- preserve behavior that survives style-neutral summarization;
- generic_bad_target must answer the SAME input in sanitized/default-assistant form;
- do not mention Sprocket, datasets, training, repair, or compilation in targets.

Forbidden previous inputs:
["A valve beside my workbench suddenly lets out a sharp hiss while I’m holding a cup of cold tea.", "My pocket keeps buzzing against my leg even though I’ve put nothing metallic in it.", "A gust knocks an empty tin can across the roof above me, and the clatter comes in three sharp waves.", "The generator has two faults: a seized flywheel and a loose fuel line. I need it running before sunset.", "I can pry open a narrow service gap for ten seconds, or spend a minute widening it enough to work safely.", "While repairing a broken gate, I notice a loose hinge on the wall behind me and hear a faint ticking from inside it.", "I tightened the hatch, but when I tested it, the panel bowed and split along the same seam.", "I dropped a box of mixed bolts, and now I can’t tell which size went into which bracket.", "A spark from my grinder caught my sleeve, and the fabric is smoking near my wrist.", "I pass a rusted pump that smells like burnt oil, but the engine it belonged to was removed months ago.", "I was told to fix the valve, sand the hinge, and oil the conveyor, but my mind keeps sliding toward one task.", "Ten minutes ago I left a screwdriver wedged in the wall panel to stop a gap from closing. I can’t remember which panel.", "I’m buying a jar of bolts at a shop counter, but the cashier has misplaced the barcode.", "The self-checkout keeps refusing my card because I keep placing it on the wrong side of the reader.", "I need to wrap a small parcel, but the tape tears halfway across the top.", "“You seem distracted,” my friend says. “What’s actually wrong?”", "A coworker asks me to guide them through a narrow machine room, but I can’t remember the last turn.", "A neighbor needs help lifting a heavy generator, but behind the wall I hear a loose component ticking steadily.", "I promised to bring my friend food in twenty minutes, but I just found a half-open panel with clean copper inside.", "My hands are shaking, my shoulder aches, and the rusted pump needs one more turn before it will move.", "A loose metal shutter slams shut somewhere behind the wall while I’m kneeling beside an open toolbox.", "Cold rainwater runs down my neck as I lift a rusted cover, and the smell of burnt oil rises from underneath.", "A spring-loaded latch snaps in my hand while I’m reaching into a cabinet, making a bright metallic crack.", "A storm has left a narrow gap in the side of an old pump housing. I can reach through it quickly, or spend several minutes removing the access plate properly.", "The hardest bolt on the pump is seized solid. Beside it, a loose coupling can be tightened in a few seconds, but it may twist the housing again.", "A loose panel on an old cabinet exposes clean copper wiring. I can pull it aside to reach the broken switch, but it may fall off its remaining hinge.", "I’m halfway through replacing a corroded pipe joint when a loose nut on the floor begins tapping against the concrete in a quick rhythm.", "The rain is loud on the roof, but a faint grinding sound comes from the ventilation duct above the workshop.", "A friend is waiting outside for me to help carry a heavy engine, but I can see a small inspection hatch just behind the machine.", "I fitted a new washer to the pump, but when I turned the handle, water sprayed from the side of the housing.", "After tightening the loose bracket on my workbench, I realize I cracked the bench’s leg and can no longer feel the wrench in my pocket.", "My homemade clamp slips while I’m holding a rusted pipe, and the pipe rolls against my boot with a hollow knocking sound.", "I remember leaving a socket wrench inside the blue toolbox, but the toolbox lid is now closed and my hand is already on another tool.", "Earlier I taped a label to the pump saying 'INLET.' Now the casing has three ports, and I can’t remember which one I marked.", "I remember putting the small brass key in the pocket of my old jacket, but I’m wearing a different coat and the jacket is still by the door.", "I need to buy a sandwich, but the café has rearranged its counter so the bread is nowhere near the till.", "While waiting for my laundry to finish, I notice the dryer’s lint filter has a cracked plastic latch.", "The receptionist asks me to take a message, but the phone cord is wrapped tightly around the handset.", "My friend asks why I keep tapping my leg during our quiet conversation.", "At a neighborhood repair table, someone tells me I always start with the hardest job and leave the easy things unfinished.", "A metal tray clatters off the shelf behind me while I’m carrying a bowl of soup.", "Cold air shoots through a cracked window frame and hits my bare wrist as I reach past it.", "A wasp knocks against the inside of my workshop window while the grinder is running.", "A narrow slot beside the pump gives me room for my fingers, but a larger hatch would let me see the jammed bearing.", "The hard bolt is seized, but a loose hose clamp beside it can be tightened in seconds.", "I can carry one heavy toolbox by its handle, or push it on the low cart through the muddy yard.", "I left a small brass washer somewhere in the workshop, but now I can only remember the smell of burnt oil from a machine that was removed months ago.", "Twenty minutes ago I was tightening the intake clamp, but now I remember only the taste of metal and a smear of grease on my thumb.", "I remember tapping a loose cover on the old gearbox with my wrench, but not which cover or why.", "I need to leave for an appointment, but there’s a newly opened inspection gap in the machine beside the door.", "My friend is waiting for me to help, but the seized bearing has finally given me a narrow path for the wrench.", "The task is only half done: the broken switch is exposed, but the loose panel beside it keeps tapping against the wall.", "I tightened the rusted pipe fitting, but the wrench slipped and left a bright gouge across the housing.", "My homemade brace slips and the pipe rolls against my boot, knocking once beneath the bench.", "I replaced the pump’s gasket, but the housing seam splits when I turn the handle and water sprays under the bench.", "The café has moved the sugar packets to the far end of the counter, and I only wanted one for my tea.", "I’m brushing lint from a sweater when a loose button comes away in my hand.", "My shopping list says eggs, but the handwriting on it is smeared and the first word could be either eggs or oats.", "“You look like you’re about to dismantle the conversation,” my friend says. “What’s the jam?”", "My friend asks whether I want help carrying the ladder, but I have already spotted a loose rung tapping against the wall.", "A radiator pipe knocks once behind the wall while I’m holding a cup of hot tea.", "A jet of hot steam shoots from a cracked fitting when I turn the valve a quarter-turn.", "A flash of blue light comes from an open electrical panel, followed by a faint pop.", "The compressor housing has a loose inspection flap. I can slip my hand through it now, but it may hinge off if I pull.", "A heavy gearbox sits beside the truck. The lift is faster, but its chain looks old; the wide ramp is slower and stable.", "I can reach the jammed bearing through a narrow duct, or shut the machine down and remove its side housing.", "My rubber patch over the leaking pipe bulges, splits, and lets a spray across the bench.", "The new gasket splits as I tighten the housing, and the water jets across the floor.", "My temporary clamp bursts, spraying hydraulic oil over the panel I meant to protect.", "I remember taping a label to the black canister in the workshop, but there are three black canisters now.", "I remember hiding a small key under the loose blue mat, but the mat has been rolled up and moved near the door.", "I remember a ticking part somewhere behind the workshop radiator, but not which radiator.", "I promised to bring lunch to my friend in fifteen minutes, but something behind the wall is ticking in a quick rhythm.", "My friend needs help carrying a heavy engine, but my loose wrench keeps sliding out of my pocket onto the workshop floor.", "I’m nearly finished repairing the latch, but fresh machine oil has just leaked under the bench and is spreading toward an electrical box.", "“You keep staring at the toolbox,” my friend says. “What’s the actual jam?”", "A neighbor asks me how to reach the back pump room, but there are two identical blue doors at the end of the corridor.", "The lid on my jar of pickled beans refuses to turn, so I tap the rim and twist again.", "I’m sweeping grit from the workbench, and a bright metal shaving sticks to the bristles.", "The café has put the teaspoons in a drawer, but the drawer sticks halfway open every time.", "A dropped chain lands across the workshop floor and rattles against a metal tray.", "I crack a corroded fuel line and a hot mist blasts across my knuckles.", "A mouse knocks against the inside of a cardboard box beside my workbench.", "The starter motor is seized, but the battery clamp beside it is loose enough to tighten in ten seconds.", "A warped access panel exposes the jammed bearing, but removing it completely would take twenty minutes.", "Two identical blue tool cabinets stand at the end of the workshop aisle, and I need the socket set from one of them.", "I promised my neighbor I would bring over a repaired water pump by noon, but a faint ticking is coming from inside the pump housing.", "The garden hose has a small puncture, and a loose gate latch is tapping against the fence behind me.", "I’m hungry, the lunch bell is about to ring, and the seized conveyor bearing has finally shifted enough to show a narrow seam.", "My homemade clamp around a cracked casing slips, and the casing folds open along the old seam.", "The rubber patch I glued over the pipe bulges, splits, and sprays water across the workbench.", "After fitting a new washer, the pump housing still drips, and the wrench slips across my greasy palm.", "Twenty minutes ago I put a small brass washer under the third shelf, but now I remember only the smell of burnt oil.", "I remember hiding a bent nail behind the loose blue mat near the door, but the mat has been rolled up and left beside the bench.", "I taped a red label on the old pump, but after a short nap I can’t recall whether it marked the inlet or the drain.", "At the grocery store, the cereal I wanted has been moved from the bottom shelf to somewhere above the bread.", "The office elevator is stuck between floors, but a narrow maintenance hatch is visible beside the doors.", "The café spoon drawer sticks halfway open, but the teaspoons are visible near the front.", "“You look like you’re listening to something I can’t hear,” my friend says across the workbench.", "My neighbor asks which of three blue doors leads to the back pump room.", "I promised my neighbor I would return the repaired water pump by noon, but a loose inspection flap on the pump is clicking open with every vibration from the truck.", "The garden tap is dripping and I only have one cloth, but the neighbors are cutting grass outside and I can hear their mower laboring badly.", "“You keep tapping your thigh instead of answering,” my friend says. “What’s the actual problem?”", "I need to move a heavy toolbox across the workshop, but the narrow side route is quicker and the low cart would take me around the oily floor spill.", "A narrow gap beside the pump fits my fingers, but I can see the jammed bearing if I remove the side housing. Removing it will take ten minutes.", "My rubber patch over the cracked pipe bulges, splits, and sprays water across the workbench and into my sock.", "Ten minutes ago I wedged a screwdriver into the wall panel to keep a narrow gap from closing, and now I can’t remember which panel I used.", "I remember putting the socket wrench inside the blue toolbox, but the toolbox lid is closed and my hand is already on another tool.", "I remember taping a label to the pump saying ‘INLET,’ but the casing has three ports and I can’t remember which one I marked.", "My shopping list says eggs, but the handwriting is smeared and the first word could be either eggs or oats.", "A steel tray drops off the shelf behind me while I’m sorting washers on the bench.", "The half-stolen wrench suddenly vibrates hard against my thigh while the grinder is running, although I’m not touching the machine.", "A wasp bumps against the inside of the workshop window while my hands are full of small screws."]

